WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.331
Yoga Class.

2
00:00:01.611 --> 00:00:06.006
Day 45 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:08.780
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:18.084
Today's goal: join a yoga class, tell the teacher about your body, follow spoken instructions, and ask for easier or harder versions of a pose.

5
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:20.287
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:21.527
Key words.

7
00:00:22.777 --> 00:00:24.143
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:46.140
Word or phrase, and Meaning. mat or block or strap: yoga equipment. pose or posture or asana: a yoga position. inhale or exhale or hold your breath: breathing. stretch or bend or twist or balance: movements. beginner or intermediate or advanced batch: class levels. modification or variation: an

9
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:56.980
easier or different way to do a pose. flexible or stiff: body condition. meditation or pranayama or relaxation (shavasana): calm practices.

10
00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.205
Part 2.

11
00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:00.786
Instructions you'll hear.

12
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.401
Here is a quick table:

13
00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:05.452
Teacher says, and What to do.

14
00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.311
Inhale, raise your arms.

15
00:01:07.591 --> 00:01:09.084
Exhale, fold forward.:

16
00:01:09.364 --> 00:01:11.817
Breathe in going up, breathe out going down.

17
00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:13.527
Hold for five breaths.:

18
00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.959
Stay in the pose.

19
00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:17.884
Keep your back straight. / Engage your core.:

20
00:01:18.164 --> 00:01:20.340
Don't bend or tighten your stomach muscles.

21
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.220
Bend your knees if it's too much.:

22
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.524
Make it easier.

23
00:01:23.804 --> 00:01:25.831
Release and come back to the centre.:

24
00:01:26.111 --> 00:01:27.369
Relax and return.

25
00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:28.908
Listen to your body.

26
00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.084
Don't push.:

27
00:01:30.364 --> 00:01:31.516
Stop if it hurts.

28
00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:33.460
Lie down for shavasana.:

29
00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.935
Relax on your back.

30
00:01:36.285 --> 00:01:37.181
Part 3.

31
00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:38.677
Questions you'll ask.

32
00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:41.911
Is this class suitable for beginners?

33
00:01:42.191 --> 00:01:43.812
Do I need to bring my own mat?

34
00:01:44.092 --> 00:01:45.159
What should I wear?

35
00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.465
I have a slipped disc or knee problem.

36
00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:49.431
Are there poses I should avoid?

37
00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:51.460
Could you show me an easier version?

38
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.255
Am I doing this correctly?

39
00:01:53.535 --> 00:01:55.412
How long should I practise each day?

40
00:01:56.762 --> 00:01:58.319
Should I eat before the class?

41
00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:00.587
Part 4.

42
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:03.491
Conversation 1: joining a yoga class.

43
00:02:04.741 --> 00:02:06.767
Here is how the conversation goes.

44
00:02:07.047 --> 00:02:09.415
Hi, I'd like to join a yoga class.

45
00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.274
I'm a complete beginner.

46
00:02:11.554 --> 00:02:12.642
Welcome!

47
00:02:12.922 --> 00:02:16.314
Our beginner batch is at 6:30 am, Monday to Friday.

48
00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:17.341
Great.

49
00:02:17.621 --> 00:02:19.562
Do I need to bring my own mat?

50
00:02:19.842 --> 00:02:22.445
We have mats, but your own is better for hygiene.

51
00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:23.663
Okay.

52
00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.759
I should mention that I have some lower back pain.

53
00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:29.709
The conversation continues.

54
00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:31.397
Thanks for telling me.

55
00:02:31.677 --> 00:02:33.299
I'll give you modifications.

56
00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:35.840
Please avoid deep forward bends for now.

57
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.912
Should I eat before class?

58
00:02:38.192 --> 00:02:41.627
Come on an empty stomach, or eat something light two hours before.

59
00:02:41.907 --> 00:02:43.016
Understood.

60
00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.597
What should I wear?

61
00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:47.547
The conversation continues.

62
00:02:47.827 --> 00:02:49.619
Comfortable, stretchy clothes.

63
00:02:49.899 --> 00:02:51.009
No jeans.

64
00:02:52.359 --> 00:02:53.319
Part 5.

65
00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:55.753
Conversation 2: during the class.

66
00:02:57.003 --> 00:02:59.030
Here is how the conversation goes.

67
00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.081
Inhale, raise both arms.

68
00:03:01.361 --> 00:03:03.238
Exhale, bend forward slowly.

69
00:03:03.518 --> 00:03:05.587
Sorry, I can't reach my toes.

70
00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:06.870
That's fine.

71
00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.198
Bend your knees a little and hold your shins.

72
00:03:09.478 --> 00:03:10.545
Like this?

73
00:03:10.825 --> 00:03:12.041
Yes, perfect.

74
00:03:12.321 --> 00:03:13.622
Keep your back long.

75
00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:15.438
Hold for five breaths.

76
00:03:16.788 --> 00:03:18.388
The conversation continues.

77
00:03:18.668 --> 00:03:19.479
Later

78
00:03:19.759 --> 00:03:21.359
Now come into tree pose.

79
00:03:21.639 --> 00:03:23.153
Balance on your right leg.

80
00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:25.396
I keep losing my balance.

81
00:03:25.676 --> 00:03:29.665
Put your foot on your ankle instead of your thigh, and look at one point in front of you.

82
00:03:29.945 --> 00:03:31.481
Oh, that's much easier.

83
00:03:32.831 --> 00:03:34.431
The conversation continues.

84
00:03:34.711 --> 00:03:35.458
Good.

85
00:03:35.738 --> 00:03:36.842
Release.

86
00:03:37.122 --> 00:03:39.640
Now lie down for shavasana and relax.

87
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.928
Part 6.

88
00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:43.232
After class.

89
00:03:44.482 --> 00:03:46.104
Thank you, that was relaxing.

90
00:03:46.384 --> 00:03:47.941
My hamstrings feel tight.

91
00:03:48.221 --> 00:03:49.245
Is that normal?

92
00:03:49.525 --> 00:03:52.512
Can you suggest a few poses to do at home before work?

93
00:03:53.862 --> 00:03:54.800
Part 7.

94
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:55.998
Practice.

95
00:03:57.248 --> 00:04:03.136
Match: inhale or exhale or hold or release, then breathe in or breathe out or stay or let go.

96
00:04:04.486 --> 00:04:05.403
Success:

97
00:04:05.683 --> 00:04:12.275
Answers. inhale = breathe in, exhale = breathe out, hold = stay, release = let go.

98
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:14.500
Part 8.

99
00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.825
Speak today.

100
00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:21.107
Do 5 minutes of stretching and say each instruction aloud in English.

101
00:04:21.387 --> 00:04:24.950
Practise telling a teacher about a health problem in one sentence.

102
00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.836
That's the end of this lesson.

103
00:04:28.116 --> 00:04:32.788
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

104
00:04:33.068 --> 00:04:39.169
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

